#: ../../../../litestar/di/provider.py:docstring of
#: litestar.di.provider.Provider.__init__:6
msgid ""
"a sync callable: In this case, sync_to_thread must be passed explicitly, to "
"define how it should be invoked. Blocking synchronous callables should pass "
"sync_to_thread=True, so they can run in a thread pool without blocking the "
"main event loop. See :doc:`/topics/sync-vs-async` for more info. A class is "
"treated as a non-blocking sync callable. It's __init__ and __new__ methods "
"should *never* block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../litestar/di/provider.py:docstring of
#: litestar.di.provider.Provider.__init__:12
msgid ""
"an async generator, yielding exactly once. The yielded value is the factory "
"value. the code after the ``yield`` will be invoked as a cleanup step when "
"this provider's DIContext closes. If the context is closing with an active "
"exception, that exception will be thrown into the generator. Cleanups are "
"guaranteed to run in reverse order they providers were invoked in. Every "
"cleanup will be invoked, even if prior cleanups raised an exception. "
"Exceptions during cleanup steps are re-raised once all cleanups have "
"completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../litestar/di/provider.py:docstring of
#: litestar.di.provider.Provider.__init__:18
msgid ""
"a sync generator, yielding exactly once, with the cleanup step of an async "
"generator. The code up to the ``yield`` runs in a worker thread, the cleanup "
"step in a thread of its own, both in one :class:`contextvars.Context`: a "
"context variable set before the ``yield`` is set after it, and set for "
"whoever resolves the provider. A context variable set where the context "
"closes is set for the cleanup step"
msgstr ""

